  "acceptance_limits": {
    "presence": "every field listed above is present in both phase records with domain, instrument and caveat; total_memory_bytes is null; the record is JSON-serializable",
    "ordering": "0 < peak_torch_allocated_bytes <= peak_torch_reserved_bytes and allocated at_start <= reserved at_start in every CUDA phase; the delta of the allocated peak is positive; the allocator peaks are exact when the test resets the peak counters first",
    "domains": "peak_process_rss_bytes has domain host, its caveat says it is not device memory, its instrument does not name torch.cuda, and its value differs from the Torch allocated peak; CPU-tile runs report the three device fields as null with a not-applicable instrument and still report the host fields",
    "disk": "for the disk-bank run, in each phase created_file_bytes == created_banks * state_bytes, scratch_disk_written_bytes and scratch_disk_read_bytes equal the StateStore counters, scratch_disk_peak_file_bytes is an integer multiple of state_bytes between 1 and state_bank_capacity, host_bank_bytes is zero, the effective rates equal bytes / seconds; in the forward phase written bytes equal created_file_bytes exactly (every owned row of every bank committed once) and in the backward phase written bytes are at least created_file_bytes",
    "host_banks": "for host-bank runs host_bank_bytes is a positive multiple of state_bytes and the scratch bytes are zero",
    "source_of_limits": "G5-02 specification: the quantities are separated and never summed; equalities are exact byte counts and no numeric tolerance applies"
  },
